  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Create a **modern, professional web application** titled:\n\n# **Animal Species Classification Using Deep Learning**\n\nBuild a complete web-based AI application where users can upload an animal image and the system predicts the animal species using a trained Deep Learning model.\n\nThe website should look like a **real AI product**, not a basic college HTML page from 2009.\n\n## 1. Main Objective\n\nCreate a web application that:\n\n* Allows users to upload an animal image\n* Processes the image\n* Sends it to a Deep Learning classification model\n* Predicts the animal species\n* Displays prediction confidence\n* Displays the top 3 predicted species\n* Provides a visual probability chart\n* Has a clean, responsive, modern interface\n\nThe model should support at least **10 animal classes**:\n\n* Dog\n* Cat\n* Lion\n* Tiger\n* Elephant\n* Horse\n* Cow\n* Deer\n* Bear\n* Monkey\n\nDesign the application so more species can easily be added later.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Recommended Technology Stack\n\n### Frontend\n\nUse:\n\n* React.js\n* TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* Framer Motion\n* Lucide React icons\n\n### Backend\n\nUse:\n\n* Python\n* FastAPI\n\n### Deep Learning\n\nUse:\n\n* TensorFlow / Keras\n* EfficientNetB0 or MobileNetV2\n* Transfer Learning\n* NumPy\n* Pillow / OpenCV\n\n### Communication\n\n```text\nReact Frontend\n       \342\206\223\nHTTP / REST API\n       \342\206\223\nFastAPI Backend\n       \342\206\223\nDeep Learning Model\n       \342\206\223\nPrediction Result\n       \342\206\223\nReact UI\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Website Design\n\nCreate a **premium AI SaaS-style interface**.\n\nUse:\n\n* Dark modern theme\n* Glassmorphism cards\n* Soft gradients\n* Rounded corners\n* Smooth animations\n* Professional typography\n* Spacious layout\n* Responsive design\n* Subtle hover effects\n* Animated loading states\n\nDo not overcrowd the UI.\n\nThe website must work properly on:\n\n* Desktop\n* Laptop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\n---\n\n# 4. Navigation Bar\n\nCreate a responsive navbar containing:\n\n**Logo**\n\n> \360\237\220\276 AnimalAI\n\nNavigation links:\n\n* Home\n* Classify\n* How It Works\n* Model\n* About\n\nRight side:\n\n**Start Classification** button\n\nOn mobile, convert navigation into a hamburger menu.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Home Page\n\nCreate a visually impressive hero section.\n\n### Hero Heading\n\n**Identify Any Animal with AI**\n\nSubheading:\n\n> Upload an animal image and let our Deep Learning model identify its species in seconds.\n\nButtons:\n\n**Classify Animal**\n\n**How It Works**\n\nAdd a large animated animal-related visual or abstract AI illustration.\n\nShow floating information cards around the hero image such as:\n\n```text\nAI Accuracy\n94%+\n\nSpecies\n10+\n\nPrediction\n< 2 sec\n```\n\nAdd subtle motion animations.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Classification Page\n\nThis is the main feature.\n\nCreate a large upload section.\n\n### Upload Card\n\nDisplay:\n\n**Upload Animal Image**\n\nSupported formats:\n\n```text\nJPG\nJPEG\nPNG\nWEBP\n```\n\nAllow:\n\n* Drag and drop\n* Browse files\n* Image preview\n\nShow an animated upload icon.\n\nAdd:\n\n**Analyze Image** button.\n\nDuring prediction show:\n\n```text\nAnalyzing Image...\n```\n\nwith an animated loader.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Prediction Result\n\nAfter prediction, display a large result card.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202             RESULT                   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202       \360\237\246\201                            \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202        LION                          \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202     Confidence: 94.72%              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202     \342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210 94.72%     \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\nDisplay:\n\n### Predicted Species\n\n**Lion**\n\n### Confidence\n\n**94.72%**\n\n### Top 3 Predictions\n\n```text\nLion        94.72%\nTiger        3.21%\nLeopard      1.14%\n```\n\nRepresent these using animated horizontal progress bars.\n\nAlso show:\n\n* Uploaded image\n* Prediction timestamp\n* Model name\n\n---\n\n# 8. Probability Visualization\n\nCreate a beautiful chart showing prediction probabilities.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nLion       \342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210 94.72%\nTiger      \342\226\210\342\226\210                   3.21%\nLeopard    \342\226\210                    1.14%\nBear       \342\226\217                    0.52%\n```\n\nUse a professional interactive chart.\n\nAnimate the chart when prediction results appear.\n\n---\n\n# 9. How It Works Section\n\nCreate a section with four steps:\n\n### Step 1\n\n**Upload Image**\n\nUser uploads an animal image.\n\n### Step 2\n\n**Preprocessing**\n\nThe system resizes and normalizes the image.\n\n### Step 3\n\n**Deep Learning**\n\nThe trained CNN / Transfer Learning model analyzes the image.\n\n### Step 4\n\n**Prediction**\n\nThe system returns the animal species and confidence score.\n\nUse animated cards connected visually.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Model Information Section\n\nCreate a professional model dashboard.\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nModel\nEfficientNetB0\n\nArchitecture\nTransfer Learning\n\nFramework\nTensorFlow / Keras\n\nClasses\n10+\n\nInput Size\n224 \303\227 224\n\nOutput\nSoftmax Classification\n```\n\nAdd a simplified architecture visualization:\n\n```text\nInput Image\n     \342\206\223\nPreprocessing\n     \342\206\223\nEfficientNetB0\n     \342\206\223\nFeature Extraction\n     \342\206\223\nGlobal Average Pooling\n     \342\206\223\nDense Layer\n     \342\206\223\nSoftmax\n     \342\206\223\nAnimal Species\n```\n\n---\n\n# 11. Supported Animals\n\nCreate an attractive grid of supported species.\n\nEach card should contain:\n\n* Animal image\n* Animal name\n* Small icon\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\360\237\220\225 Dog\n\360\237\220\210 Cat\n\360\237\246\201 Lion\n\360\237\220\205 Tiger\n\360\237\220\230 Elephant\n\360\237\220\216 Horse\n\360\237\220\204 Cow\n\360\237\246\214 Deer\n\360\237\220\273 Bear\n\360\237\220\222 Monkey\n```\n\nCards should have hover animations.\n\n---\n\n# 12. About Section\n\nDisplay:\n\n### About AnimalAI\n\nExplain that the system uses Deep Learning and image classification to identify animal species from uploaded images.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Purpose\n* Technology\n* Model\n* Dataset\n* Classification capability\n\nDo not make unsupported claims such as \342\200\23499.9% accurate.\342\200\235\n\n---\n\n# 13. Backend API\n\nBuild a FastAPI backend.\n\nCreate endpoint:\n\n```text\nPOST /predict\n```\n\nThe API must:\n\n1. Receive uploaded image\n2. Validate image format\n3. Preprocess image\n4. Load trained model\n5. Run prediction\n6. Calculate probabilities\n7. Return top 3 predictions\n\nExample JSON response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"prediction\": \"Lion\",\n  \"confidence\": 94.72,\n  \"top_predictions\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Lion\",\n      \"confidence\": 94.72\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Tiger\",\n      \"confidence\": 3.21\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Leopard\",\n      \"confidence\": 1.14\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nHandle errors properly.\n\nReturn useful messages for:\n\n* Invalid image\n* Unsupported format\n* Missing model\n* Server error\n* Empty upload\n\n---\n\n# 14. Deep Learning Model\n\nImplement the model using **EfficientNetB0 Transfer Learning**.\n\nThe backend should load:\n\n```text\nmodels/animal_classifier.keras\n```\n\nPreprocess the image to:\n\n```text\n224 \303\227 224\n```\n\nPerform:\n\n* Resizing\n* Normalization\n* Tensor conversion\n* Prediction\n* Softmax probability calculation\n\nReturn the top 3 predictions.\n\nKeep the model-loading logic separate from the API routes.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Backend Structure\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nbackend/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 model.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 preprocessing.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 config.py\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 animal_classifier.keras\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n# 16. Frontend Structure\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nfrontend/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Hero.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 UploadBox.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PredictionResult.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProbabilityChart.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 HowItWorks.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ModelInfo.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Footer.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Home.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Classify.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Model.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 About.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html\n```\n\nKeep components modular and reusable.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Frontend API Integration\n\nCreate a service for calling the FastAPI backend.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrontend\n   \342\206\223\nUpload image\n   \342\206\223\nPOST /predict\n   \342\206\223\nFastAPI\n   \342\206\223\nTensorFlow model\n   \342\206\223\nJSON response\n   \342\206\223\nDisplay prediction\n```\n\nUse proper loading and error states.\n\n---\n\n# 18. User Experience\n\nThe application should feel fast and polished.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Smooth page transitions\n* Loading animations\n* Skeleton states where useful\n* Button hover effects\n* Drag-and-drop animation\n* Image preview animation\n* Prediction result animation\n* Responsive design\n* Toast notifications for errors\n\nDo not use excessive animations that make the interface annoying.\n\nHumans already have enough distractions.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Extra Features\n\nAdd these features where practical:\n\n### Recent Predictions\n\nDisplay the latest predictions locally in the browser.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nRecent Predictions\n\nLion       94.7%\nDog        91.4%\nElephant   96.2%\n```\n\n### Clear Button\n\nAllow users to remove the uploaded image and start again.\n\n### Try Another Image\n\nAfter prediction, provide:\n\n**Classify Another Image**\n\nbutton.\n\n### Sample Images\n\nProvide several sample animal images that users can click to test the classifier.\n\n---\n\n# 20. UI Components\n\nCreate reusable components for:\n\n* Buttons\n* Cards\n* Progress bars\n* Upload area\n* Prediction results\n* Navigation\n* Charts\n* Alerts\n* Loading indicators\n\nUse consistent spacing and typography throughout the website.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Color and Visual Style\n\nUse a sophisticated AI-inspired design.\n\nPreferred style:\n\n* Dark background\n* White text\n* Soft purple/blue gradient accents\n* Glass-effect cards\n* Subtle borders\n* Soft shadows\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Excessively bright colors\n* Cluttered layouts\n* Huge amounts of text\n* Generic Bootstrap appearance\n\n---\n\n# 22. Important Requirements\n\nThe generated application must:\n\n* Be fully functional\n* Use real API communication\n* Use a real Deep Learning prediction pipeline\n* Have clean component structure\n* Have proper error handling\n* Have responsive design\n* Have no fake prediction results\n* Have no hardcoded random confidence values\n* Have consistent API response types\n* Have proper TypeScript types\n* Be easy to run locally\n\n---\n\n# 23. Final Deliverables\n\nGenerate the complete source code for:\n\n### Frontend\n\n* React + TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* Framer Motion\n* All components\n* All pages\n* API integration\n\n### Backend\n\n* FastAPI\n* Model loading\n* Image preprocessing\n* Prediction endpoint\n* Error handling\n\n### Deep Learning\n\n* EfficientNetB0 model\n* Prediction logic\n* Class mapping\n\n### Configuration\n\nProvide:\n\n* `package.json`\n* `requirements.txt`\n* `.env.example`\n\nDo **not** create a README file.\n\n---\n\n# 24. Running the Project\n\nProvide exact commands to run the project.\n\nBackend:\n\n```bash\ncd backend\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n```\n\nFrontend:\n\n```bash\ncd frontend\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nMake sure the frontend API URL can be configured using an environment variable.\n\n---\n\n# 25. Final Instruction to the Coding AI\n\nGenerate the project **file by file**, with the complete code for every required file.\n\nDo not provide pseudo-code.\n\nDo not omit important files.\n\nEnsure every import, component, route, API endpoint, model path, and environment variable is consistent.\n\nThe final website should look like a **professional AI-powered animal recognition platform** suitable for a college Deep Learning mini-project demonstration.\n Include a responsive dashboard, image upload functionality, and real-time classification results.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Create a **modern, professional web application** titled:\n\n# **Animal Species Classification Using Deep Learning**\n\nBuild a complete web-based AI application where users can upload an animal image and the system predicts the animal species using a trained Deep Learning model.\n\nThe website should look like a **real AI product**, not a basic college HTML page from 2009.\n\n## 1. Main Objective\n\nCreate a web application that:\n\n* Allows users to upload an animal image\n* Processes the image\n* Sends it to a Deep Learning classification model\n* Predicts the animal species\n* Displays prediction confidence\n* Displays the top 3 predicted species\n* Provides a visual probability chart\n* Has a clean, responsive, modern interface\n\nThe model should support at least **10 animal classes**:\n\n* Dog\n* Cat\n* Lion\n* Tiger\n* Elephant\n* Horse\n* Cow\n* Deer\n* Bear\n* Monkey\n\nDesign the application so more species can easily be added later.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Recommended Technology Stack\n\n### Frontend\n\nUse:\n\n* React.js\n* TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* Framer Motion\n* Lucide React icons\n\n### Backend\n\nUse:\n\n* Python\n* FastAPI\n\n### Deep Learning\n\nUse:\n\n* TensorFlow / Keras\n* EfficientNetB0 or MobileNetV2\n* Transfer Learning\n* NumPy\n* Pillow / OpenCV\n\n### Communication\n\n```text\nReact Frontend\n       \342\206\223\nHTTP / REST API\n       \342\206\223\nFastAPI Backend\n       \342\206\223\nDeep Learning Model\n       \342\206\223\nPrediction Result\n       \342\206\223\nReact UI\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Website Design\n\nCreate a **premium AI SaaS-style interface**.\n\nUse:\n\n* Dark modern theme\n* Glassmorphism cards\n* Soft gradients\n* Rounded corners\n* Smooth animations\n* Professional typography\n* Spacious layout\n* Responsive design\n* Subtle hover effects\n* Animated loading states\n\nDo not overcrowd the UI.\n\nThe website must work properly on:\n\n* Desktop\n* Laptop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\n---\n\n# 4. Navigation Bar\n\nCreate a responsive navbar containing:\n\n**Logo**\n\n> \360\237\220\276 AnimalAI\n\nNavigation links:\n\n* Home\n* Classify\n* How It Works\n* Model\n* About\n\nRight side:\n\n**Start Classification** button\n\nOn mobile, convert navigation into a hamburger menu.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Home Page\n\nCreate a visually impressive hero section.\n\n### Hero Heading\n\n**Identify Any Animal with AI**\n\nSubheading:\n\n> Upload an animal image and let our Deep Learning model identify its species in seconds.\n\nButtons:\n\n**Classify Animal**\n\n**How It Works**\n\nAdd a large animated animal-related visual or abstract AI illustration.\n\nShow floating information cards around the hero image such as:\n\n```text\nAI Accuracy\n94%+\n\nSpecies\n10+\n\nPrediction\n< 2 sec\n```\n\nAdd subtle motion animations.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Classification Page\n\nThis is the main feature.\n\nCreate a large upload section.\n\n### Upload Card\n\nDisplay:\n\n**Upload Animal Image**\n\nSupported formats:\n\n```text\nJPG\nJPEG\nPNG\nWEBP\n```\n\nAllow:\n\n* Drag and drop\n* Browse files\n* Image preview\n\nShow an animated upload icon.\n\nAdd:\n\n**Analyze Image** button.\n\nDuring prediction show:\n\n```text\nAnalyzing Image...\n```\n\nwith an animated loader.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Prediction Result\n\nAfter prediction, display a large result card.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202             RESULT                   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202       \360\237\246\201                            \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202        LION                          \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202     Confidence: 94.72%              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202     \342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210 94.72%     \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\nDisplay:\n\n### Predicted Species\n\n**Lion**\n\n### Confidence\n\n**94.72%**\n\n### Top 3 Predictions\n\n```text\nLion        94.72%\nTiger        3.21%\nLeopard      1.14%\n```\n\nRepresent these using animated horizontal progress bars.\n\nAlso show:\n\n* Uploaded image\n* Prediction timestamp\n* Model name\n\n---\n\n# 8. Probability Visualization\n\nCreate a beautiful chart showing prediction probabilities.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nLion       \342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210\342\226\210 94.72%\nTiger      \342\226\210\342\226\210                   3.21%\nLeopard    \342\226\210                    1.14%\nBear       \342\226\217                    0.52%\n```\n\nUse a professional interactive chart.\n\nAnimate the chart when prediction results appear.\n\n---\n\n# 9. How It Works Section\n\nCreate a section with four steps:\n\n### Step 1\n\n**Upload Image**\n\nUser uploads an animal image.\n\n### Step 2\n\n**Preprocessing**\n\nThe system resizes and normalizes the image.\n\n### Step 3\n\n**Deep Learning**\n\nThe trained CNN / Transfer Learning model analyzes the image.\n\n### Step 4\n\n**Prediction**\n\nThe system returns the animal species and confidence score.\n\nUse animated cards connected visually.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Model Information Section\n\nCreate a professional model dashboard.\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nModel\nEfficientNetB0\n\nArchitecture\nTransfer Learning\n\nFramework\nTensorFlow / Keras\n\nClasses\n10+\n\nInput Size\n224 \303\227 224\n\nOutput\nSoftmax Classification\n```\n\nAdd a simplified architecture visualization:\n\n```text\nInput Image\n     \342\206\223\nPreprocessing\n     \342\206\223\nEfficientNetB0\n     \342\206\223\nFeature Extraction\n     \342\206\223\nGlobal Average Pooling\n     \342\206\223\nDense Layer\n     \342\206\223\nSoftmax\n     \342\206\223\nAnimal Species\n```\n\n---\n\n# 11. Supported Animals\n\nCreate an attractive grid of supported species.\n\nEach card should contain:\n\n* Animal image\n* Animal name\n* Small icon\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\360\237\220\225 Dog\n\360\237\220\210 Cat\n\360\237\246\201 Lion\n\360\237\220\205 Tiger\n\360\237\220\230 Elephant\n\360\237\220\216 Horse\n\360\237\220\204 Cow\n\360\237\246\214 Deer\n\360\237\220\273 Bear\n\360\237\220\222 Monkey\n```\n\nCards should have hover animations.\n\n---\n\n# 12. About Section\n\nDisplay:\n\n### About AnimalAI\n\nExplain that the system uses Deep Learning and image classification to identify animal species from uploaded images.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Purpose\n* Technology\n* Model\n* Dataset\n* Classification capability\n\nDo not make unsupported claims such as \342\200\23499.9% accurate.\342\200\235\n\n---\n\n# 13. Backend API\n\nBuild a FastAPI backend.\n\nCreate endpoint:\n\n```text\nPOST /predict\n```\n\nThe API must:\n\n1. Receive uploaded image\n2. Validate image format\n3. Preprocess image\n4. Load trained model\n5. Run prediction\n6. Calculate probabilities\n7. Return top 3 predictions\n\nExample JSON response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"prediction\": \"Lion\",\n  \"confidence\": 94.72,\n  \"top_predictions\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Lion\",\n      \"confidence\": 94.72\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Tiger\",\n      \"confidence\": 3.21\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"Leopard\",\n      \"confidence\": 1.14\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nHandle errors properly.\n\nReturn useful messages for:\n\n* Invalid image\n* Unsupported format\n* Missing model\n* Server error\n* Empty upload\n\n---\n\n# 14. Deep Learning Model\n\nImplement the model using **EfficientNetB0 Transfer Learning**.\n\nThe backend should load:\n\n```text\nmodels/animal_classifier.keras\n```\n\nPreprocess the image to:\n\n```text\n224 \303\227 224\n```\n\nPerform:\n\n* Resizing\n* Normalization\n* Tensor conversion\n* Prediction\n* Softmax probability calculation\n\nReturn the top 3 predictions.\n\nKeep the model-loading logic separate from the API routes.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Backend Structure\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nbackend/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 model.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 preprocessing.py\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 config.py\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 animal_classifier.keras\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n# 16. Frontend Structure\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nfrontend/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Hero.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 UploadBox.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PredictionResult.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProbabilityChart.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 HowItWorks.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ModelInfo.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Footer.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Home.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Classify.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Model.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 About.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html\n```\n\nKeep components modular and reusable.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Frontend API Integration\n\nCreate a service for calling the FastAPI backend.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrontend\n   \342\206\223\nUpload image\n   \342\206\223\nPOST /predict\n   \342\206\223\nFastAPI\n   \342\206\223\nTensorFlow model\n   \342\206\223\nJSON response\n   \342\206\223\nDisplay prediction\n```\n\nUse proper loading and error states.\n\n---\n\n# 18. User Experience\n\nThe application should feel fast and polished.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Smooth page transitions\n* Loading animations\n* Skeleton states where useful\n* Button hover effects\n* Drag-and-drop animation\n* Image preview animation\n* Prediction result animation\n* Responsive design\n* Toast notifications for errors\n\nDo not use excessive animations that make the interface annoying.\n\nHumans already have enough distractions.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Extra Features\n\nAdd these features where practical:\n\n### Recent Predictions\n\nDisplay the latest predictions locally in the browser.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nRecent Predictions\n\nLion       94.7%\nDog        91.4%\nElephant   96.2%\n```\n\n### Clear Button\n\nAllow users to remove the uploaded image and start again.\n\n### Try Another Image\n\nAfter prediction, provide:\n\n**Classify Another Image**\n\nbutton.\n\n### Sample Images\n\nProvide several sample animal images that users can click to test the classifier.\n\n---\n\n# 20. UI Components\n\nCreate reusable components for:\n\n* Buttons\n* Cards\n* Progress bars\n* Upload area\n* Prediction results\n* Navigation\n* Charts\n* Alerts\n* Loading indicators\n\nUse consistent spacing and typography throughout the website.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Color and Visual Style\n\nUse a sophisticated AI-inspired design.\n\nPreferred style:\n\n* Dark background\n* White text\n* Soft purple/blue gradient accents\n* Glass-effect cards\n* Subtle borders\n* Soft shadows\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Excessively bright colors\n* Cluttered layouts\n* Huge amounts of text\n* Generic Bootstrap appearance\n\n---\n\n# 22. Important Requirements\n\nThe generated application must:\n\n* Be fully functional\n* Use real API communication\n* Use a real Deep Learning prediction pipeline\n* Have clean component structure\n* Have proper error handling\n* Have responsive design\n* Have no fake prediction results\n* Have no hardcoded random confidence values\n* Have consistent API response types\n* Have proper TypeScript types\n* Be easy to run locally\n\n---\n\n# 23. Final Deliverables\n\nGenerate the complete source code for:\n\n### Frontend\n\n* React + TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* Framer Motion\n* All components\n* All pages\n* API integration\n\n### Backend\n\n* FastAPI\n* Model loading\n* Image preprocessing\n* Prediction endpoint\n* Error handling\n\n### Deep Learning\n\n* EfficientNetB0 model\n* Prediction logic\n* Class mapping\n\n### Configuration\n\nProvide:\n\n* `package.json`\n* `requirements.txt`\n* `.env.example`\n\nDo **not** create a README file.\n\n---\n\n# 24. Running the Project\n\nProvide exact commands to run the project.\n\nBackend:\n\n```bash\ncd backend\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n```\n\nFrontend:\n\n```bash\ncd frontend\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nMake sure the frontend API URL can be configured using an environment variable.\n\n---\n\n# 25. Final Instruction to the Coding AI\n\nGenerate the project **file by file**, with the complete code for every required file.\n\nDo not provide pseudo-code.\n\nDo not omit important files.\n\nEnsure every import, component, route, API endpoint, model path, and environment variable is consistent.\n\nThe final website should look like a **professional AI-powered animal recognition platform** suitable for a college Deep Learning mini-project demonstration.\n Include a responsive dashboard, image upload functionality, and real-time classification results.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
