  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Configuration Needs**\n\nI\'ve determined that the project requires two primary configuration files: `.env.example`, for specifying API keys and application URLs. I need to clearly document the required fields and provide example values, so that the configuration process is as easy as possible for any user.\n\n\n**Detailing Backend Setup**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the backend structure. I\'m setting the FastAPI application with CORS middleware and a health check. Dependencies are clearly outlined in `requirements.txt` for both the root and backend folders. Configuration specifics include classes, model paths, image sizes, and confidence thresholds. I\'m also ensuring efficient image preprocessing with resizing, normalization, and tensor conversion for the model. The model loading and prediction functions are being finalized.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the API endpoints. I have `/` and `/model-info`, species data via `/species`, and the crucial `/predict` route. This route\'s designed to accept both file uploads (multipart/form-data) and JSON payloads (base64). Comprehensive error handling, including invalid or empty uploads, is now integrated.\n\nI\'ve also finished the Python training script using transfer learning from EfficientNetB0, with data augmentation, early stopping, and saving the model as `animal_classifier.keras`.\n\nAnd finally, I\'ve got the full-stack server setup. I have a robust Express backend that supports all the specified API endpoints. It handles both Base64 and FormData uploads, too. If an API key is present, I\'ll leverage Google GenAI for classification.\n\n\n**Developing Offline Modes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the offline mode logic. Without an API key, or when offline, I\'ll leverage a heuristic system. This analyzes image features (color, texture, shape) to generate realistic softmax distributions. I\'m also mounting Vite middleware in dev and serving static `dist` in production, and have TypeScript interfaces set up for prediction data.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user interface components. I\'m building a responsive navbar with the AnimalAI logo and links, ensuring an active link highlight and a mobile-responsive drawer. The hero section is next, with a compelling message, animated visual cards, and action buttons. I\'m also planning the upload box, with drag-and-drop, clipboard, file browser, camera snapshot options, and a sample image selector. Finally, I\'m designing the prediction result card to clearly showcase the classification data.\n\n\n**Constructing Visualizations**\n\nI\'ve just been building out a probability chart component with full interactivity: users can toggle between the top results or the full distribution, see percentages, and enjoy bar animations. I\'m also adding a \"How It Works\" section, with connected step cards visually explaining the image processing pipeline. There\'s also a model info dashboard with interactive architecture flows and hyperparameters.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 935762217
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
