  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Frontend Modules**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the frontend modules meticulously. I\'m focusing on crafting clear TypeScript interfaces within `src/types.ts` to manage predictions, animal metadata, model information, history, and sample images. Additionally, I\'m building detailed animal data in `src/data/animals.ts` to represent the complete information. I have a good handle on how the components and files should be made.\n\n\n**Constructing Animal Data**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `src/data/animals.ts` file with detailed animal classes. I\'ve included emoji icons, descriptions, scientific names, and typical weights/lifespans. I\'m focusing on their taxonomic classification and sourcing reliable Unsplash URLs for sample images in `src/data/sampleImages.ts`. This ensures users have immediate access to test images.\n\nI\'m also setting up the API service in `src/services/api.ts`, which includes upload handling, connection to the prediction endpoint, base64 helper functions, local caching, and error formatting.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the user interface. I\'m building key components like the image upload card, camera capture interface, and file/sample image pickers. I\'m visualizing the image preview with a scanning laser animation and \"Analyze Image\" button with a loading state. I\'m prioritizing the high-impact `PredictionResult.tsx` card, integrating animated emoji, species details, confidence percentages, progress bars, and visual feature display. I\'m also planning the probability bar chart.\n\n\n**Detailing Model Information**\n\nI\'m now detailing the model information component (`src/components/ModelInfo.tsx`). I\'m developing spec summary cards highlighting EfficientNetB0, transfer learning, and TensorFlow/Keras. I\'m also constructing an interactive visual architecture diagram with layer descriptions. Additionally, I\'m integrating a confusion matrix and dataset metrics. I\'m also working on supporting animal grids with photos, names, dietary badges, and quick test buttons. I\'m adding recent prediction history.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 166269821
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
