    thinking: "**Constructing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to build out the UI components now. Specifically, the focus is on `src/components/Navbar.tsx`. The navigation bar will include a gradient pill logo that displays \"AnimalAI\" and a status dot indicating model online. The navbar will also feature links to Home, Classify, How It Works, and Model pages.\n\n\n**Adding Hero Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the Hero component, crafting the introduction. It will have a clear heading \"Identify Any Animal with AI\" with a concise subheading. Two buttons are planned: \"Classify Animal\" and \"How It Works\". I\'m also sketching out floating glass cards to highlight key AI specs like accuracy and speed. I am also working on a visual illustration of the AI scanning process.\n\n\n**Developing Prediction Results**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `PredictionResult` component. A large card will display the results, including a big emoji and species name. It will show confidence levels and top predictions with animated bars. I\'m also including the uploaded image, timestamp, and a description of salient visual features. There will be information on taxonomy, diet, habitat, and a fun fact. Buttons to \"Classify Another Image\" and \"Clear\" are included, with confetti for high-confidence detections!\n\n\n**Detailing Workflow & Model**\n\nI\'m now detailing the `HowItWorks` component, outlining a 4-step pipeline: upload, preprocessing (image resizing and normalization), deep learning (EfficientNetB0 extraction), and prediction (softmax ranking). I\'m simultaneously working on the `ModelInfo` component, creating a model dashboard with EfficientNetB0 details, a simplified architecture flow diagram, and training benchmarks. Also, I\'m working on the `SupportedAnimals` component with species cards and \"Test Classifier\" buttons and a `RecentPredictions` component using local storage.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 666863864
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
