    response: "I have designed and built the **Animal Species Classification Using Deep Learning** web application, featuring a dark AI SaaS interface, real-time inference pipeline, and comprehensive model diagnostics:\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Key Highlights & Architecture\n\n- **Visual Identity & Design System**: Crafted a dark modern theme with glassmorphism cards, soft cyan/indigo glowing accents, responsive typography using *Plus Jakarta Sans* and *JetBrains Mono*, and subtle motion states.\n- **Classification Engine**:\n  - Supports **10 core animal classes**: Dog \360\237\220\225, Cat \360\237\220\210, Lion \360\237\246\201, Tiger \360\237\220\205, Elephant \360\237\220\230, Horse \360\237\220\216, Cow \360\237\220\204, Deer \360\237\246\214, Bear \360\237\220\273, and Monkey \360\237\220\222.\n  - Preprocessing pipeline enforcing **224 \303\227 224 \303\227 3** image resizing and tensor normalization.\n  - Dual backend capability: Live full-stack server endpoint (`/api/predict` and `/predict`) alongside a standalone **FastAPI + TensorFlow / EfficientNetB0** backend in the `backend/` directory.\n- **Image Input & Interactive Testing**:\n  - Drag-and-drop zone, file explorer, webcam photo snapshot capture, and a **Sample Animal Shelf** for instant 1-click test classifications.\n- **Prediction Result & Probability Visualization**:\n  - High-visibility result card featuring the predicted animal species, prominent confidence percentage, animated horizontal progress bars, Top 3 ranked candidate predictions, and salient visual features identified.\n  - Interactive **Probability Distribution Chart** visualizing normalized Softmax scores across all 10 classes.\n- **Model Dashboard & Pipeline Sections**:\n  - **How It Works**: 4-stage visual flow explaining image upload, Lanczos tensor preprocessing, convolutional feature extraction, and Softmax categorical classification.\n  - **Model Architecture**: Detailed neural network graph showing the *EfficientNetB0 backbone*, *Global Average Pooling 2D*, *Dropout/Dense layers*, and *Softmax head*.\n  - **Supported Animals Grid**: Interactive cards displaying taxonomy, habitat, dietary classification, and quick test buttons.\n  - **Recent History**: Local session persistence displaying latest classifications with confidence ratings and re-inspection capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\222\273 Running the Project Locally\n\n#### Backend (FastAPI + Python)\n```bash\ncd backend\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n```\n\n#### Frontend (React + Vite)\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```"
    thinking: "**Reviewing Built Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now in the review phase, meticulously going through the built components. I\'m focusing on ensuring all the requirements are met, starting with the title: \"Animal Species Classification Using Deep Learning\". Currently, I\'m specifically evaluating the web application\'s functionality. It should allow users to upload images through drag and drop, file browsing, and even camera snapshots.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and built the **Animal Species Classification Using Deep Learning** web application, featuring a dark AI SaaS interface, real-time inference pipeline, and comprehensive model diagnostics:\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Key Highlights & Architecture\n\n- **Visual Identity & Design System**: Crafted a dark modern theme with glassmorphism cards, soft cyan/indigo glowing accents, responsive typography using *Plus Jakarta Sans* and *JetBrains Mono*, and subtle motion states.\n- **Classification Engine**:\n  - Supports **10 core animal classes**: Dog \360\237\220\225, Cat \360\237\220\210, Lion \360\237\246\201, Tiger \360\237\220\205, Elephant \360\237\220\230, Horse \360\237\220\216, Cow \360\237\220\204, Deer \360\237\246\214, Bear \360\237\220\273, and Monkey \360\237\220\222.\n  - Preprocessing pipeline enforcing **224 \303\227 224 \303\227 3** image resizing and tensor normalization.\n  - Dual backend capability: Live full-stack server endpoint (`/api/predict` and `/predict`) alongside a standalone **FastAPI + TensorFlow / EfficientNetB0** backend in the `backend/` directory.\n- **Image Input & Interactive Testing**:\n  - Drag-and-drop zone, file explorer, webcam photo snapshot capture, and a **Sample Animal Shelf** for instant 1-click test classifications.\n- **Prediction Result & Probability Visualization**:\n  - High-visibility result card featuring the predicted animal species, prominent confidence percentage, animated horizontal progress bars, Top 3 ranked candidate predictions, and salient visual features identified.\n  - Interactive **Probability Distribution Chart** visualizing normalized Softmax scores across all 10 classes.\n- **Model Dashboard & Pipeline Sections**:\n  - **How It Works**: 4-stage visual flow explaining image upload, Lanczos tensor preprocessing, convolutional feature extraction, and Softmax categorical classification.\n  - **Model Architecture**: Detailed neural network graph showing the *EfficientNetB0 backbone*, *Global Average Pooling 2D*, *Dropout/Dense layers*, and *Softmax head*.\n  - **Supported Animals Grid**: Interactive cards displaying taxonomy, habitat, dietary classification, and quick test buttons.\n  - **Recent History**: Local session persistence displaying latest classifications with confidence ratings and re-inspection capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\222\273 Running the Project Locally\n\n#### Backend (FastAPI + Python)\n```bash\ncd backend\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n```\n\n#### Frontend (React + Vite)\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```"
